# Real faces. These never go into version control.
#
# The photos in images/, images-acne/ and images-acne-tight/ are of real
# people who sent them so a vendor could be evaluated. That is not consent to
# publish them, and a git history is permanent in a way a folder is not: once
# pushed, a face is recoverable from the history even after the file is
# deleted.
#
# The manifests are kept. They record which Fitzpatrick band each image was
# assigned and what the vendor returned, which is the part that carries the
# evidence -- the finding survives without the face.
images/*.jpg
images/*.jpeg
images/*.png
images-acne/*.jpg
images-acne/*.jpeg
images-acne-tight/*.jpg
images-acne-tight/*.jpeg
images-smoke/*.jpg
images-smoke/*.jpeg
!**/manifest.csv

# Raw vendor responses contain the SAME faces, base64-encoded inside
# `face_maps`. Excluding the photos while committing these would publish the
# faces in a less obvious format, which is worse, not better.
results/raw/
results/maps/

# Build output
*.exe
